---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Zcompressor vs Sejda - Free Unlimited Sejda Alternative | Compress PDF"
  description="Compare Zcompressor and Sejda. Discover why Zcompressor is a completely unlimited, secure alternative to Sejda for compressing your PDF documents without file size or page caps."
  ogUrl="https://zcompressor.com/vs/sejda"
>
  <!-- JSON-LD FAQ Schema for SEO -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do Zcompressor's limits compare to Sejda?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>Sejda imposes strict free limitations: a maximum of 3 tasks per day, files under 50MB in size, and documents under 200 pages. Zcompressor is completely free and has no daily task quotas, page limits, or file volume restrictions.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Zcompressor safer for company documents than Sejda?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Sejda requires uploading your documents to their servers where they remain stored for up to 2 hours. Zcompressor processes your PDFs locally inside your browser cache. Your documents never traverse the web or touch remote hard drives, providing absolute confidentiality.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Zcompressor require installation or account registration?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>No. Zcompressor runs directly inside your web browser sandbox and does not require registration, accounts, emails, or installation of any sort. You can use it completely anonymously.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <Header />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas-soft text-ink py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto">
      <!-- Eyebrow & Title -->
      <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
        <span
          class="text-caption-mono font-mono text-link-deep dark:text-cyan-deep uppercase tracking-wider block mb-3 animate-fade-in"
        >
          Product Comparison
        </span>
        <h1
          class="text-display-lg md:text-display-xl text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-1.5px] md:tracking-[-2.4px] mb-4"
        >
          Zcompressor vs Sejda.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-body-lg text-body text-balance">
          Analyzing service limitations, cloud retention policies, and client-side processing advantages.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview Section -->
      <section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
          Sejda is an online PDF management utility. While it offers a broad suite of editing features, free tier users are highly restricted by daily quotas (3 files/day), file size ceilings (50MB), page limit caps (200 pages), and server upload security policies.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
          Zcompressor provides a lightweight, local alternative optimized for fast, secure batch processing without daily counters or page restrictions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Side-by-Side Comparison Table -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.96px] mb-6">
          Feature Breakdown.
        </h2>
        <div class="border border-hairline rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-level-2 bg-canvas">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-mute uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Feature</th>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-ink font-semibold uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Zcompressor</th>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-mute uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Sejda</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Daily Task Quota</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Unlimited (No caps)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">3 Tasks per day</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Maximum File Size</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Unlimited (Device RAM dependent)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">50 MB max per file</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Maximum Page Cap</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Unlimited</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">200 Pages max per file</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Server Retention</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">0 seconds (Local sandbox)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Stored in cloud for 2 hours</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Batch Queue support</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Yes (Parallel thread execution)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Requires premium upgrade</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Deep Dive Comparisons -->
      <section class="space-y-10 mb-16">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] mb-3">
            Bypass page and size restrictions.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
            Sejda enforces strict page caps (200 pages) and file size caps (50MB) for free users. If you attempt to upload a book, a legal folder, or a high-resolution architectural layout, the system rejects it, requesting subscription payments.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
            Zcompressor compiles its document layout libraries locally. Because processing relies on your browser’s own compilation sandbox, there are no artificial page or document caps. You are free to optimize large books or files directly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-lg bg-canvas border border-hairline p-6 shadow-level-3">
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] mb-3">
            Data security: why local processing is cleaner.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Sejda retains uploaded PDFs on its remote hard drives for up to two hours post-compression. This brief storage window still presents data interception, leak, and server exploit risks.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
            Zcompressor guarantees absolute privacy. Because all processing executes in-browser, no data resides on a remote server. You can compress legal briefs, corporate data, and patient reports without concern for cloud data retention policies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12 mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.96px] mb-8">
          Frequently Asked Questions.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Can Zcompressor compress image-heavy PDFs?</h4>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Yes, Zcompressor excels at optimizing scanned documents and images. It resizes resolution structures and re-encodes image assets inside the document stream completely locally.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Does Zcompressor store cookies or tracking profiles?</h4>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              No. Zcompressor uses browser LocalStorage purely to persist your UI preference (dark vs. light mode). We do not build profiles, track your device, or sell advertising telemetry.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Call to Action -->
      <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold mb-6">Compress high-page PDFs without caps.</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="/compress-pdf"
            class="px-6 h-[48px] bg-primary text-on-primary text-button-lg rounded-pill hover:bg-black transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center shadow-level-3 hover:scale-[1.02] duration-200"
          >
            Start Compressing
          </a>
          <a
            href="/vs"
            class="px-6 h-[48px] bg-canvas text-ink border border-hairline text-button-lg rounded-pill hover:bg-canvas-soft transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center shadow-level-2 hover:scale-[1.02] duration-200"
          >
            View Alternatives
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
